  "summary": "Dearborn City Council unanimously approved a $720,000 five-year contract with Axon's Fusus to give police access to opt-in private camera feeds, drawing concerns from civil liberties advocates about potential surveillance of pro-Palestinian protesters and immigrants. Officials emphasized the system lacks facial recognition and that the city does not own the footage.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Dearborn City Council recently unanimously approved $720,000 for a five-year contract for police to use Axon's Fusus program that gains access to the private camera feeds of businesses and individuals who opt into the program.",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "The Fusus system is not equipped for the integration of facial recognition technology.",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    },
    {
      "quote": "They really do want to sort of establish themselves as being like an entire ecosystem of police surveillance technology",
      "paragraph_idx": 21
    }
